// Brokkr-managed — installed by scripts/setup-host-patching.sh only onto the Ubuntu
// hosts the owner approved in BROKKR_REGULAR_UPDATE_HOSTS (Grimnir ADR-009: regular OS
// updates, guarded reboots). Any other host keeps the distribution's security
// baseline, and the script removes this file from it.
//
// The distribution's own 50unattended-upgrades (release, -security, ESM) stays in
// place and is never overwritten by Brokkr; apt merges list-valued options across
// apt.conf.d files, so these patterns are added beside it:
//   * Ubuntu -updates  - regular bug-fix updates. Deliberately NOT -backports and
//                        NOT -proposed. Phased updates are honoured by
//                        unattended-upgrades, so a phased package waits its turn.
//   * Tailscale        - a network-exposed daemon that should not wait for a person;
//                        its Ubuntu repository uses the release codename as channel.
// Every repository is matched by exact origin, label and codename / channel; a
// channel that is not listed here is never admitted. A pattern that matches no
// configured repository is a no-op.
// Reboots are never done here; see the guarded-reboot job.
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=Ubuntu,archive=${distro_codename}-updates,label=Ubuntu";
        "origin=Tailscale,label=Tailscale,codename=${distro_codename}";
};
